{"abstract":"This one-day workshop seeks to bring together design researchers that have different orientations and practices for futures and futur- ing to unpack the role of futuring across design, design artefacts, and designers. Our goal in this workshop is to use examples of established futures to engage with and reflect on questions around the role of futures in HCI/design. We believe that there is a common thread between work from many different researchers, but that the people doing that work are spread across different disciplines and geographical locations. To that end, this workshop will assem- ble researchers working with different methods and approaches to futures in design and will aim to identify core challenges and opportunities for futures in HCI.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jenkins, Tom","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Boer, Laurens","Kun, Peter","Howell, Noura","Wong, Richmond","Campo Woytuk, Nadia","Søndergaard, Maria Louise Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759409"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["AHO The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway","All Global Affiliations","Georgia Institute of Technology","KTH Royal Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Design Futuring","Design research","Futures"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mapping futures and futuring in hci design","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/%2010.1145/3656156.3658384","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759409","identifier":[{"id":"85198906038","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-91abe117-12cd-4c3b-9943-34ab75c4ac66"],"keyword":["design futuring","design research","futures"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5E149DA731F91BC1D38C3C0F1DE88B83"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/105488248/2024_Jenkins_et_al_-_Mapping_Futures_and_Futuring_in_HCI_Design.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/%2010.1145/3656156.3658384","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"aho the oslo school of architecture and design norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AHO The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"kunpau","last":"Kun","locid":"f30d35c6-4320-476f-8506-481764e6009e","name":"Kun, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-0778-7662","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Noura","key":"howellpau","last":"Howell","name":"Howell, Noura","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Richmond","key":"wongpau","last":"Wong","name":"Wong, Richmond","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nadia","key":"campowoytukpau","last":"Campo Woytuk","name":"Campo Woytuk, Nadia","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Louise Juul","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","name":"Søndergaard, Maria Louise Juul","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3656156.3658384","pages":"458-461","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Designing Interactive Systems Conference 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198906038"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-91abe117-12cd-4c3b-9943-34ab75c4ac66"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mapping Futures and Futuring in HCI/Design","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759409","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Sleep technologies promise optimised sleep by tracking sleep cy- cles or by affecting sleep environment. This paper expands sleep technology to address more complex notions of sleep, proposing dream technology as a path for reflective practices that focus on nightly dreams rather than hours slept. Because dreams are bizarre and hard to grasp, we turn to speculative design practices in an RtD framework to investigate the nature of dreaming. This process pro- duced the ‘dream sticker machine’, a design proposal that visualises a user’s dreams with an AI image generator. This tangible dream trace becomes sharable in both public and personal spaces. This proposal formed the basis of a probe to how people might imagine their dreams taking form in the real world, and led to ideas for how the materials of dreams might be taken up as part of design research practice.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Krogh Bønlykke, Sofie","Amalie Lind Madsen, Kamma","Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S02-083.43-803629"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","end":"2024-07-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-07-01","title":"2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Design fiction","Dreams","Human centred computing","Interaction design","Probes","Research through Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"taking the bizarre seriously dreams as a material for interaction design","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3661562","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-083.43-803629","identifier":[{"id":"85200377455","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-21ba2b8b-516c-46e4-ab19-a686cb0615e2","itu-d82e5256-b462-4a1d-bb79-88231a34a00e"],"keyword":["Design Fiction","Human-centred computing","Interaction design","Interaction design process and method","Probes","Research through design","dreams"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3848F3CFBD974D4B05E0DABF533993B8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/105488141/2024_B_nlykke_et_al_-_Taking_the_Bizarre_Seriously.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/772358333/3643834.3661562.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3661562","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Service Systems Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"no