{"abstract":"Prototyping is a complex process of navigating a chaotic design space. Especially when there are few criteria for success, it is often difficult for a designer to know what direction to follow. We argue that prototyping can be considered as a process of sensemaking driven by finding the right expression of a design goal. To illustrate this, we present the case study of the aural-visualiser 1000, a functional refined prototype that resulted from an open-ended design project. Using its process as an example, we abstract important expressions that informed the design and prototyping of the aural-visualiser 1000, pointing to when the conception of the project changed and how that affected our making sense of the design space. We reflect on this design process to articulate productive pivots and tensions that led to the finished artefact.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718851"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Expression","Listening","Presence","Prototyping","Sensemaking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prototyping as making sense of expressions","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100700224/2023_Padalak_Jenkins_Prototyping_as_making_sene_of_expressions.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718851","ids":["itu-4907f5e7-06f2-406b-aabe-1b780a6167b3"],"keyword":["Prototyping","expression","listening","presence","sensemaking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2928EE14D3F97251F56E9734F9454B39"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100700224/2023_Padalak_Jenkins_Prototyping_as_making_sene_of_expressions.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Abildgaard","key":"padalakpau","last":"Padalak","locid":"17ebd58d-ffad-4a6f-923d-a0118d0056b0","name":"Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Design Research Society","status":"p","subtitle":"From Abstractness to Concreteness","title":"EKSIG 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4907f5e7-06f2-406b-aabe-1b780a6167b3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prototyping as making sense of expressions","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718851","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Envisioning alternative futures and desirable worlds is a core element of design that must be cultivated, especially when a deep transition of practices, values, and power is necessary for vibrant and just future lifeworlds. In this paper, we contribute towards fabulation as an approach for design futuring that foregrounds feminist commitments and more-than-human concerns. Analyzing two fabulation case studies around biodata and bodily fluids, we offer three themes based on our process of developing these fabulations: how they engage materials, how they work to trouble temporalities, and how they cultivate imagination. We argue for the emerging potential of fabulation as an approach for open-ended, joyful design futuring, mobilizing speculative storytelling to foreground absent or neglected relations when imagining alternative lifeworlds.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Juul Søndergaard, Marie Louise","Campo Woytuk, Nadia","Howell, Noura","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Helms, Karey","Jenkins, Tom","Sanches, Pedro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718921"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["AHO The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway","All Global Affiliations","Georgia Institute of Technology","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Umeå University"],"keyword":["Critical Feminist Technoscience","Design Futuring","Fabulation","Research through Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fabulation as an approach for design futuring","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100700021/2023_S_ndergaard_et_al_Fabulation_as_an_Approach_for_Design_Futuring.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718921","ids":["itu-d2cdd24b-1c04-4094-a8e7-1c480e885a51"],"keyword":["Critical Feminist Technoscience","Design Futuring","Fabulation","Research through Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-59CB0325CF8664E9CEDF12EC8223DDEA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100700021/2023_S_ndergaard_et_al_Fabulation_as_an_Approach_for_Design_Futuring.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3563657.3596097","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"aho the oslo school of architecture and design norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AHO The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"georgia institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"umeå university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Umeå University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Louise","key":"juulsøndergaardpau","last":"Juul Søndergaard","name":"Juul Søndergaard, Marie Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nadia","key":"campowoytukpau","last":"Campo Woytuk","name":"Campo Woytuk, Nadia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Noura","key":"howellpau","last":"Howell","name":"Howell, Noura","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karey","key":"helmspau","last":"Helms","name":"Helms, Karey","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"sanchespau","last":"Sanches","name":"Sanches, Pedro","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3563657.3596097","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Designing Interactive Systems (DIS '23)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d2cdd24b-1c04-4094-a8e7-1c480e885a51"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fabulation as an Approach for Design Futuring","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=s