{"abstract":"This project uses research through design to explore how metadata could be used as a design material to create inheritable artefacts that make personal legacy experiential. Metadata is produced as traces of life, and by designing artifacts that capture and represent these traces, interaction design offers the possibility to experience the everyday practices of someone else as they are passed on and inherited. We use interviews with people interested in data practices, memorializing, and who have experienced grief to find themes and insights for designing with metadata as well as for legacy. Based on these, we developed the prototype Anekdota, a handheld metadata detector that lets an inheritor experience bequeathed location metadata. From a series of think-aloud walks, Anekdota was tested with participants to reveal sensitizing concepts for designing for metadata, and imaginative leaps for how this metadata may become a part of future legacy practices.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Michael Nørgaard","Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677314"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Legacy","Metadata","Prototyping","Research through Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing anekdota investigating personal metadata for legacy","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3544548.3581495","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677314","identifier":[{"id":"85160006037","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-62b86b48-de53-4c3b-8cb2-59edd0a9b0bd"],"keyword":["Legacy","Metadata","Prototyping","Research through Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EE2AA46C6D10B702D6A0EE346D73D0D5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3544548.3581495","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/98230202/2023_J_rgensen_and_Jenkins_Metadata_as_Legacy.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Nørgaard","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Michael Nørgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3544548.3581495","pages":"1-14","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2023 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160006037"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-62b86b48-de53-4c3b-8cb2-59edd0a9b0bd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing Anekdota: Investigating Personal Metadata for Legacy","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677314","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"A growing number of design researchers explore engagement with and through biodata. To help make sense of this growing space, we synthesize three emergent themes: (1) expanding notions of biodata and bodies, (2) attending to a greater diversity of human bodies and experiences with biodata, and (3) biodata collaborations between human and non-human bodies. We illustrate these themes with selected design examples. From this synthesis, we develop three interconnected fabulations reimagining alternative engagements with biodata: Weaving Alongside, Diffracting Selves, and Collective Affect. Our discussion unpacks conceptual work of the fabulations, offering invitations for design research to explore alternative ways of living and knowing together with biodata.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Sanches, Pedro","Jenkins, Tom","Howell, Noura","Boer, Laurens","Bitzouni, Afroditi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384356"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia Institute of Technology","Umeå University"],"keyword":["Biodata","Bodies","Design research","Diffraction","Fabulation","Futuring","More than human"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fabulating biodata futures for living and knowing together","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3532106.3533477","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384356","identifier":[{"id":"85133602322","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["