{"abstract":"This paper explores how the smartphone's form could be designed to help users establish more intentional usage patterns. A research through design approach that was based in design fiction principles resulted in three design proposals and scenarios, the Planning Phone, the Parasite Phone, and the Placeful Phone. These were evaluated in a focus group and analysed to develop a deeper understanding of how design researchers and developers can use ideas of authorship, barriers and norms to support intentional smartphone use.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Stepanovic, Mila","Boer, Laurens","Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382596"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Polytechnic University of Milan"],"keyword":["Smartphone Intentional use Design Research Interaction Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reconfiguring the smartphone to support intentional use","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87114576/nordichi22_37.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382596","identifier":[{"id":"85140887109","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-598d5d49-7caf-4e8f-a0df-31b06095f2b0"],"keyword":["Smartphone, Intentional use, Design Research, Interaction Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-525DC3A9A4B88F765F842A0ECFFE574F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87114576/nordichi22_37.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"polytechnic university of milan","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Milan","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mila","key":"stepanovicpau","last":"Stepanovic","name":"Stepanovic, Mila","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3546155.3546675","isbn":["9781450396998"],"pages":"1","place":"Aarhus, Denmark","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '22: Nordic Human-Computer Interaction Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140887109"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-598d5d49-7caf-4e8f-a0df-31b06095f2b0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reconfiguring the Smartphone to Support Intentional Use","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382596","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The aural-visualiser 1000 is a prototype that reorients a user towards understanding the world from an auditory perspective instead of a primarily visual one. By attending to everyday audio instead of vision, the device asks the user to pay attention to the world in a more embodied way. Developed as a means of experimenting with the capacity of physical interaction design to support being present in the world differently, it records audio from everyday life and creates mementos for later reflection and interpretation. The mementos, paper receipts with abstract sound visualizations on them, offer a means of remembering experiences as they were to be there, instead of as they were recorded through image or video.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","Gehrchen, Thea Emilie","Hansen, Søren Smedegaard","Pedersen, Peter Langgard","Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382659"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["RtD attention presence senses images interaction design aes thetics expressions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aural visualiser 000000001000 physical interaction design for materializing moments","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87114792/nordichiadjunct22_48.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382659","identifier":[{"id":"85139872027","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5ccd4eb5-1d7b-4986-bf6c-5e24ab5694d8"],"keyword":["RtD, attention, presence, senses, images, interaction design, aes- thetics, expressions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4DFB09B2AD7E24FB98DB9900AEF51C00"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87114792/nordichiadjunct22_48.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Abildgaard","key":"padalakpau","last":"Padalak","locid":"17ebd58d-ffad-4a6f-923d-a0118d0056b0","name":"Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thea Emilie","key":"gehrchenpau","last":"Gehrchen","name":"Gehrchen, Thea Emilie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Smedegaard","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Søren Smedegaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Langgard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Peter Langgard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3547522.3547722","isbn":["9781450394482"],"pages":"1-3","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '22: Adjunct Proceedings of the 2022 Nordic Human-Computer Interaction Conference"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139872027"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5ccd4eb5-1d7b-4986-bf6c-5e24ab5694d8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"aural-visualiser 1000: physical interaction design for materializing moments","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382659","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Recent design research has shown an interest in diffraction and agential realism, which promise to offer generative alternatives when designing with data that resist treating data as objective or neutral. We explore engaging diffractively with ‘lived data’to surface felt and prospective aspects of data as it is entangled in everyday lives of designers. This paper presents five biodata-based case studies demonstrating how design researchers can create knowledge about human bodies and behaviors via strategies that allow them to engage data diffractively. These studies suggest that designers can find insights for designing with data as it is lived by working with it in a slow, open-ended fashion that leaves room for messiness and time for discovering difference. Finally, we discuss the role of ambiguous, open-ended data interpretations to help surface different meanings and entanglements of data in everyday lives.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Sanches, Pedro","Howell, Noura","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Jenkins, Tom","Helms, Karey"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382760"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia Institute of Technology","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Umeå University"],"keyword":["Being with","Biodata","Bodies","Collaboration","Data","Design","Design research","Empathy","Material","More than human"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diffraction in action designerly explorations of agential realism through lived data","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":[