{"abstract":"Aural-visualiser 1000 is an interactive system for recording the world around you. Like a camera that captures sounds instead of images, it is meant to develop memories that are focused on what it was like to be in a moment. Aural-visualiser 1000 critiques an image-centered society, particularly how the image has become the dominant form of representing human experience. Collections of photos have become a replacement memory that end up never being looked at. Often, taking a photograph or finding the right angle for a video replaces being present in the world. Focusing on audio requires a user to relate to their world and engage actively in finding things worth noticing. In creating a memento from the sound, av1000 records a memory that can be reviewed later. This requires active participation to reconstruct a meaningful experience. The system argues for interaction design that goes beyond tapping fingers on glass towards exploring the surrounding world intentionally.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384268"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Attention presence senses images interaction design RtD"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"being in the world with the aural visualiser 000000001000","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85140883379","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384268","identifier":[{"id":"85140883379","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-cd1a7a2f-8626-45e4-93a6-80bc3ead406b"],"keyword":["Attention, presence, senses, images, interaction design, RtD"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-59546C5A1C36C3811822D4E40C3674AD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Abildgaard","key":"padalakpau","last":"Padalak","locid":"17ebd58d-ffad-4a6f-923d-a0118d0056b0","name":"Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3546155.3547281","isbn":["9781450396998"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Nordic Human-Computer Interaction Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140883379"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cd1a7a2f-8626-45e4-93a6-80bc3ead406b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Being in the world with the aural-visualiser 1000","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384268","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Creative confidence is a concept that has been popularly linked to design thinking in more generalist interaction design education. Based on an analysis of creative confidence, however, we propose that Speculative and Critical Design practices (SCD) can be a better perspective for developing creative confidence in aspiring designers. We present how we have taught two subsequent SCD courses as part of a short 2-year generalist interaction design master’s programme. Based on the outcome of selected student projects, course evaluations, and personal reflections, we articulate the promises and pitfalls of using SCD to foster creative confidence.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384294"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Creative Confidence","Creative Self Beliefs","Creative Self Image","Design","Education","Interaction design","Speculative and Critical Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fostering creative confidence with scd in interaction design education","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.55612/s-5002-051-012","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384294","identifier":[{"id":"85129412031","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ce8c63cd-76ac-4a45-b35b-dcc9fe8b6bbb"],"keyword":["Creative Confidence","Creative Self-Beliefs","Creative Self-Image","Design","Education","Interaction Design","Speculative and Critical Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D927E74668E1F865180122F0E5844270"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90369441/51_12.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.55612/s-5002-051-012","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.55612/s-5002-051-012","issn":["18269745","22832998"],"issn_org":["18269745"],"issue":"51","journal":"Interaction Design and Architecture","pages":"270-302","paperid":"12","publisher":"Interaction Design and Architecture(s)","status":"p","title":"Interaction Design and Architecture","title_org":"Interaction Design & Architecture(s)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129412031"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ce8c63cd-76ac-4a45-b35b-dcc9fe8b6bbb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fostering Creative Confidence with SCD in Interaction Design Education","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384294","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a research through design project to develop and interpret speculative smart home technologies for cohousing communities—Cohousing IoT. Fieldwork at multiple sites coupled to a constructive design research process led to three prototypes designed for cohousing communities, a Cohousing Radio, a Physical RSVP, and Participation Scales. These were brought back to the communities that inspired them as a form of evaluation, but also to generate new understandings of designing for cohousing. In discussing how they understand these prototypes, it offers an account of how research though design generates knowledge that is specific to the conditions and issues that matter to those communities. This contributes to design research more broadly in two ways. First, it demonstrates how contemporary ideas of smart home technology are or could be made relevant to broader ways of living in the future. Second, it provides an example of how a design research process can serve to uncover community values, issues, and goals.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384009"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Community research","Design research","Prototypes","Public design","Publics","Research through Design","cohousing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cohousing iot technology design for life in community","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/mti5030014","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384009","identifier":[{"id":"85104004039","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-bba90c58-cf75-4782-8f7d-485a3ba93f02"],"keyword":["Community research","cohousing","design research","prototypes","public design","publics","research through design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E2AB5A115A96DC7D10D8852B8B29A672"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/mti5030014","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85832874/mti_05_00013.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/mti5030014","issn":["24144088"],"issue":"3","journal":"Multimodal Technologies and Interaction","paperid":"14","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Multimodal Technologies and Interaction","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104004039"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bba90c58-cf75-4782-8f7d-485a3ba93f02"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cohousing IoT : Technology Design for Life In Community","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384009","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Remote sensing can advance the work of the Circumpolar Biodiversity Monitoring Program through monitoring of satellite-derived terrestrial and marine physical and ecological variables. Standardized data facilitate an unbiased comparison across variables and environments. Using MODIS standard products of land surface temperature, percent snow covered area, NDVI, EVI, phenology, burned area, marine chlorophyll, CDOM, sea surface temperature, and marine primary productivity, significant trends were observed in almost all variables between 2000 and 2017. Analysis of seasonal data revealed significant breakpoints in temporal trends. Within the terrestrial environment, data showed significant increasing trends in land surface temperature and NDVI. In the marine environment, significant increasing trends were detected in primary productivity. Significantly earlier onset of green up date was observed in bioclimate subzones C&E and longer end of growing season in B&E. Terrestrial and marine parameters showed similar rates of change with unidirectional change in terrestrial and significant directional and magnitude shifts in marine.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jenkins, Liza K.","Barry, Tom","Bosse, Karl R.","Currie, William S.","Christensen, Tom","Longan, Sara","Shuchman, Robert A.","Tanzer, Danielle","Taylor, Jason J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-237809"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jenkins, Liza K."],"country":["Iceland","United States"],"glorg":["Alaska Department of Natural Resources","All Global Affiliations","Michigan Technological University","United States Geological Survey","University of Iceland","University of Michigan"],"keyword":["Arctic","MODIS","Remote sensing","Satellite","Time series"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"satellite based decadal change assessments of pan arctic environments","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6989704/pdf/13280_2019_Article_1249.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-237809","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6989704","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85074830722","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31686338","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-bdf6a75f-662a-4a02-b31b-c52c33a350b0"],"keyword":["Arctic","MODIS","Remote sensing","Satellite","Time series"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FBBF309342E2CEF77C7C5D20368DD191"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6989704/pdf/13280_2019_Article_1249.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"michigan technological university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Michigan Technological University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of michigan","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Michigan","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"is","key":"university of iceland","loc":["Iceland","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Iceland","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Arctic Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"alaska department of natural resources","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Alaska Department of Natural Resources","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"united states geological survey","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"United States Geological Survey","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Liza K.","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","name":"Jenkins, Liza K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"barrypau","last":"Barry","name":"Barry, Tom","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karl R.","key":"bossepau","last":"Bosse","name":"Bosse, Karl R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"William S.","key":"curriepau","last":"Currie","name":"Currie, William S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tom","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"c2b982ca-b8de-47c1-b339-145ce573ef02","name":"Christensen, Tom","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"longanpau","last":"Longan","name":"Longan, Sara","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert A.","key":"shuchmanpau","last":"Shuchman","name":"Shuchman, Robert A.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Danielle","key":"tanzerpau","last":"Tanzer","name":"Tanzer, Danielle","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Jason J.","key":"taylorpau","last":"Taylor","name":"Taylor, Jason J.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31686338"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s13280-019-01249-z","issn":["0044